@page "/operate/resources/new"

<section class="console-page">
    <div class="console-page-heading">
        <p class="console-kicker">Operate / Resources</p>
        <h1>Create Resource</h1>
        <p>Resources can start from an owned table, uploaded file, or one-time remote-service migration. Migration creates Console-owned metadata instead of proxying, syncing, or mirroring the remote service.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="console-panel-grid">
        <article class="console-panel">
            <p class="console-kicker">Table</p>
            <h2>Database Table</h2>
            <p class="console-muted">Bind a table or view from an existing connection, validate fields and geometry, then publish through a service slot.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="console-panel">
            <p class="console-kicker">File</p>
            <h2>Upload File</h2>
            <p class="console-muted">Stage a file import, inspect inferred fields, fix validation issues, and create a canonical data resource.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="console-panel">
            <p class="console-kicker">Migration</p>
            <h2>One-Time Remote Service Migration</h2>
            <p class="console-muted">Copy schema, metadata, and supported features into a native resource. The remote service remains a source, not a proxy target.</p>
        </article>
    </div>
</section>
